  "sat_solver_calls": 0,
  "scope": "For a nonnegative matrix H and a nonnegative commutator D = S*H-H*S, every entry D[i,j] vanishes if some power of H has a positive [j,i] entry. The six weak reversed digit-conversion matrix inequalities therefore are equalities at every such returning pair for H=A+B+E+F+G, including every diagonal entry. If the five-digit sum is irreducible, all six matrix inequalities are equalities. The affine interface assumes only the six weak swaps and digit nonnegativity. It does not claim equality of offset comparisons, existence of a certificate, vanishing of the eligible gaps, or the Collatz conjecture.",
  "status": "PASS"
